    q(31,"AmpC patient case","JM has bacteremia caused by AmpC-producing Enterobacter cloacae. It is susceptible to ceftriaxone, cefepime, piperacillin–tazobactam, and meropenem. JM takes valproic acid for seizures. Which antibiotic is most appropriate?",("Ceftriaxone","Cefepime","Piperacillin–tazobactam","Meropenem"),(1,),"Cefepime is stable against AmpC and avoids the major carbapenem–valproic acid interaction.","AmpC plus valproate points to cefepime."),
